questions.question:
Let  X = \left[ {\matrix{ 0 & 1 & 0  \cr 0 & 0 & 1  \cr 0 & 0 & 0  \cr

} } \right],\,Y = \alpha I + \beta X + \gamma {X^2}  and $Z = {\alpha ^2}I - \alpha \beta X + ({\beta ^2} - \alpha \gamma ){X^2}$, $\alpha$, $\beta$, $\gamma \in$ R. If  {Y^{ - 1}} = \left[ {\matrix{ {\frac{1}{5}} & {{{ - 2} \over 5}} & {\frac{1}{5}}  \cr 0 & {\frac{1}{5}} & {{{ - 2} \over 5}}  \cr 0 & 0 & {\frac{1}{5}}  \cr

} } \right] , then ($\alpha - \beta + \gamma$)^{2} is equal to ____________.

questions.explanation:
$\because $X = \left[ {\matrix{ 0 & 1 & 0  \cr 0 & 0 & 1  \cr 0 & 0 & 0  \cr

} } \right] 

$\therefore ${X^2} = \left[ {\matrix{ 0 & 0 & 1  \cr 0 & 0 & 0  \cr 0 & 0 & 0  \cr

} } \right] 

$\therefore $Y = \alpha I + \beta X + \gamma {X^2}\left[ {\matrix{ \alpha  & \beta  & \gamma   \cr 0 & \alpha  & \beta   \cr 0 & 0 & \alpha   \cr

} } \right] 

$\because Y\,.\,{Y^{ - 1}} = I \therefore $\left[ {\matrix{ \alpha  & \beta  & \gamma   \cr 0 & \alpha  & \beta   \cr 0 & 0 & \alpha   \cr

} } \right]\left[ {\matrix{ {\frac{1}{5}} & {{{ - 2} \over 5}} & {\frac{1}{5}}  \cr 0 & {\frac{1}{5}} & {{{ - 2} \over 5}}  \cr 0 & 0 & {\frac{1}{5}}  \cr

} } \right]\left[ {\matrix{ 1 & 0 & 0  \cr 0 & 1 & 0  \cr 0 & 0 & 1  \cr

} } \right] 

$\therefore $\left[ {\matrix{ {\frac{\alpha}{5}} & {{{\beta  - 2\alpha } \over 5}} & {{{\alpha  - 2\beta  + \gamma } \over 5}}  \cr 0 & {\frac{\alpha}{5}} & {{{\beta  - 2\alpha } \over 5}}  \cr 0 & 0 & {\frac{\alpha}{5}}  \cr

} } \right] = \left[ {\matrix{ 0 & 0 & 0  \cr 0 & 1 & 0  \cr 0 & 0 & 1  \cr

} } \right] 

$\therefore \alpha$ = 5, $\beta$ = 10, $\gamma$ =15

$\therefore$ ($\alpha - \beta + \gamma$)^{2} = 100
